# npm resolves registries per scope, not per package — but that is not a problem
# here, because GitHub Packages serves **every** `@alfresco` package we need.
#
# Verified empirically (Phase 0, re-confirmed Phase 2) by downloading each tarball
# with only this mapping in place:
#   @alfresco/adf-extensions@9.0.0                 30,927 bytes
#   @alfresco/js-api@10.0.0                       592,491 bytes
#   @alfresco/adf-core@9.0.0                      924,425 bytes
#   @alfresco/adf-hx-content-services@7.20.0-...  379,417 bytes
#
# adf-extensions, adf-core and js-api are published to public npm *as well*, which
# is what makes the two-registry reading tempting. adf-hx-content-services is the
# only one that is GitHub-Packages-exclusive, so pointing the scope here is the
# mapping that satisfies all four and keeps Phase 3 unblocked.
#
# Consequence to keep in mind: `@alfresco/adf-extensions` is a production
# dependency, so CI now needs SATORI_GH_READONLY_TOKEN to hold read:packages
# access to the Alfresco org — not just to @hylandsoftware.
@alfresco:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
@hylandsoftware:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${SATORI_GH_READONLY_TOKEN}
